| **G3 – QueryPatientRetrievalCapability**     | Ask whether the inpatient can retrieve a meal from the robot’s tray.                                        | `-`                                              | Query         | “Can inpatient retrieve meal from tray?”                | AND          | The decision between tray-delivery and direct placement depends on this information.                                                                        |    OK                |                    |                    |
| **G4 – DecideDeliveryMethod**                | Choose the delivery method (tray or direct).                                                                | `FALLBACK(G4.1,G4.2)`                            | Perform       | –                                                       | OR           | If tray-delivery fails (e.g., patient cannot retrieve), the fallback is direct placement.                                                                   |   OK                 |                    |                    |
| **G4.1 – TrayDelivery**                      | Deliver the meal to the patient’s tray.                                                                     | `;`                                              | Perform       | –                                                       | AND          | Tray delivery requires both dish retrieval and patient notification.                                                                                        |   OK                 |                    |                    |
| **G4.1.1 – RetrieveDishes**                  | Retrieve dirty dishes from the room.                                                                        | `FALLBACK(G4.1.1.1,FALLBACK(G4.1.1.2,G4.1.1.3))` | Perform       | –                                                       | OR           | The robot can do it alone, with another robot, or with a human.                                                                                             | Achieve. Target condition: all dishes were retrieved.                   |                    |                    |
| **G4.1.1.1 – UnassistedDishRetrieval**       | Robot retrieves dishes by itself.                                                                           | `-`                                              | Perform       | –                                                       | AND          | When the robot has sufficient manipulation skill and the room is accessible.                                                                                |  OK                  |                    |                    |
| **G4.1.1.2 – RobotCooperativeDishRetrieval** | Robot cooperates with another robot to retrieve dishes.                                                     | `-`                                              | Perform       | –                                                       | AND          | Needed when a single robot cannot lift or carry the dishes.                                                                                                 |  OK                  |                    |                    |
| **G4.1.1.3 – HumanCooperativeDishRetrieval** | Robot cooperates with a human to retrieve dishes.                                                           | `-`                                              | Perform       | –                                                       | AND          | Needed when a human is present and can help.                                                                                                                | OK                   |                    |                    |
| **G4.1.2 – NotifyPatientToRetrieveMeal**     | Inform the patient that the meal is ready on the tray.                                                      | `-`                                              | Perform       | –                                                       | AND          | The patient must know when to collect the meal.                                                                                                             |  OK                  |                    |                    |
| **G4.2 – DirectDelivery**                    | Place the meal directly on the patient’s table.                                                             | `-`                                              | Perform       | –                                                       | AND          | Direct placement is the alternative when the patient cannot retrieve from a tray.                                                                           |  OK                  |                    |                    |
| **G4.2.1 – PlaceMealOnTable**                | Place the meal on the inpatient’s table using a special manipulation skill.                                 | `-`                                              | Perform       | –                                                       | AND          | Requires the robot’s manipulation capability.                                                                                                               |  OK                  |                    |                    |
| **G5 – OpenRoomDoor**                        | Open the patient’s room door.                                                                               | `FALLBACK(G5.1,G5.2)`                            | Perform       | –                                                       | OR           | The robot can open the door itself or request a human.                                                                                                      |  OK                  |                    |                    |
| **G5.1 – RobotOpenDoor**                     | Robot opens the door.                                                                                       | `-`                                              | Perform       | –                                                       | AND          | When the door is operable by the robot.                                                                                                                     | OK                   |                    |                    |
| **G5.2 – HumanOpenDoor**                     | Human opens the door.                                                                                       | `-`                                              | Perform       | –                                                       | AND          | When a human is present and willing.                                                                                                                        |   OK                 |                    |                    |
